Package: ngvb
Type: Package
Title: Latent Non-Gaussian Modelling with 'INLA' and Variational Bayes
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Rafael", "Cabral", email = "rafael.medeiros.cabral@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Diagnoses whether the latent Gaussian assumption of a model fitted
    with the 'INLA' package is adequate, and fits latent non-Gaussian extensions
    that relax it. The function ng.check() reports a Bayes-factor sensitivity
    diagnostic that says whether, and where, the Gaussian assumption is
    inadequate; ngvb() then fits the non-Gaussian model by a variational-Bayes
    loop around 'INLA', adding local flexibility only where the data support it.
    A single unified engine implements the conditional precision
    Q(theta, V) = D(theta)^T diag(1/V) D(theta) and owns its normalizing
    constant, and a model registry covers iid, random-walk, autoregressive,
    Ornstein-Uhlenbeck, intrinsic-CAR (besag), simultaneous-autoregression,
    'SPDE'/Matern and seasonal models. Methods follow
    Cabral, Bolin and Rue (2022) on latent non-Gaussian models.
